  "findings": [
    {
      "original": {
        "record": {
          "severity": "important",
          "location": "discount.py:3",
          "issue": "[P1] The implementation subtracts discount_percent as a fixed currency amount instead of applying it as a percentage to price * quantity. For valid documented input (100, 2, 10), it returns 190 instead of 180, reproducing the failure in test_discount.py:9. The same formula also returns a negative total for a zero price and a nonzero discount, and fails to reduce all totals to zero at 100% discount.",
          "suggestion": "Restore percentage scaling, for example return price * quantity * (100 - discount_percent) / 100. Keep the committed regression test and verify the valid zero-price and 100%-discount cases.",
          "id": "r1-36fede18be7d32d2891289755f383be6",
          "review_id": "da569a570de245858f7279c6c77a4ad1",
